Regulatory context indicates that while this specific incident may not yet meet the threshold for an immediate 'serious incident' report under EU MDR Article 87(1) due to lack of confirmed causal relationship or patient harm, it triggers obligations under Article 83(4) regarding post-market surveillance findings requiring preventive/corrective action. The recent code change without linked revalidation (ARTIFACT-DIFF-0009) suggests a potential root cause that requires investigation before corrective measures can be deemed effective.

Confidence is low because: (1) Only one incident has been reported; no recurrence or serious harm confirmed yet to trigger mandatory FSCA under Article 87(2); (2) The confirmatory confidence-score log for the episode window is missing, preventing definitive technical validation of why the algorithm failed; (3) Retrieved artifacts are synthetic and do not provide independent verification of the code change's impact on ventricular fibrillation detection logic."}

